        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Moroni 9:9",
        "book": "Moroni",
        "chapter": 9,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "And after they had done this thing, they did murder them in a most cruel manner, torturing their bodies even unto death; and after they have done this, they devour their flesh like unto wild beasts, because of the hardness of their hearts; and they do it for a token of bravery.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 67,
            "end": 72,
            "text": "TG Cruelty."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Cruelty.",
            "prettyString": "TG Cruelty",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Cruelty",
                "entryId": "tg-cruelty",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Moroni 9:10",
        "book": "Moroni",
        "chapter": 9,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "O my beloved son, how can a people like this, that are without civilization—",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Moroni 9:11",
        "book": "Moroni",
        "chapter": 9,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "(And only a few years have passed away, and they were a civil and a delightsome people)",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Moroni 9:12",
        "book": "Moroni",
        "chapter": 9,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "But O my son, how can a people like this, whose delight is in so much abomination—",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 48,
            "end": 55,
            "text": "2 Ne. 9:9 (8–9); Jacob 3:11."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Moroni 9:13",
        "book": "Moroni",
        "chapter": 9,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "How can we expect that God will stay his hand in judgment against us?",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 32,
            "end": 36,
            "text": "2 Sam. 24:16; Alma 10:23."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "2 Sam. 24:16; Alma 10:23.",
            "prettyString": "2 Samuel 24:16; Alma 10:23",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "2samuel",
                "chapters": [
                  {
